> Hmm.  So polymorphed pets don't gain experience?  The cockatrice won't
> eventually become a "large" cockatrice?

There are several ways pets can gain levels.  The ones I know of are
killing monsters (gaining a max HP per kill, and a corresponding hit
die for every 8), eating wraith corpses, and drinking potions of gain
level.

The lore I'm familiar with says that pets won't gain levels through
combat greater than half their initial hit dice, unless they can
progress into a larger monster size.  Cockatrices are at the top of
their particular progression sequence, and they don't have many hit
dice by default, so they'll never become particularly useful.  I don't
think they eat, and they certainly don't drink potions, so once you get
deep into the dungeon you'll likely find you won't get much use out of
your favorite pet lizard-chicken -- while he's alive, at least.

